# Line endings. This repository is edited on Windows and its containers run on
# Linux, so the two must be kept apart deliberately.
#
# The shell script is the one that actually breaks: a checkout with CRLF gives
# the container `#!/bin/sh\r`, and Linux reports it as
# `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` - an error that names a file that looks correct
# in every editor. Dockerfiles, YAML and nginx config are pinned for the same
# reason, being read only inside Linux images.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.svg   text
*.otf   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pptx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.pdf   binary
